WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.382 --> 00:00:01.215
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.215 --> 00:00:02.520
- [Narrator] Renault and
Nissan have announced

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.230
a long plan overhaul of their more than

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.180
20 year old alliance.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.520
- We are now ready to move our partnership

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.563
obviously to a new era.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.590
- [Narrator] The partnership
withstood the ousting

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:18.270
of a leader, a global
pandemic and growing pains.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.160
The CEOs of both companies spoke

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.830
to the Wall Street Journal about
their restructured alliance

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.770
and what it means for investors
and the global industry.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.050
- Importance is how we can transform right

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.770
under this difficult circumstances
that we are facing today.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.650
- So we are trying to create
a company that is much

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.420
more agile, more oriented

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.320
to innovation because
technology is evolutionary.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.520
- [Narrator] But first,
how did we get here?

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:44.708
(camera clicking)

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:47.040
The partnership dates to
1999 when Renault took a more

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.070
than one third stake in
Nissan, which was struggling.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:50.903
- They were in this kind

00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:53.550
of marriage where they
had to get the agreement

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.100
of the other if they wanted to cooperate.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.240
- [Narrator] At the
height of the Alliance,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.980
they were joined by Mitsubishi Motors

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.780
and had a combined sales of more than

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.343
10 million vehicles a year.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.790
But beneath the surface,
Nissan saw the partnership

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.490
as uneven with Renault
holding a controlling stake

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.020
in the Japanese car maker.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.520
On the other hand, Renault felt it

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.530
wasn't getting enough for its large stake.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.190
There was also a clash of
corporate cultures, for years.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.740
Industry veteran Carlos
Ghosn headed both companies

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.540
and was able to smooth out differences

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.253
with his forceful personality.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.530
But when Ghosn was arrested

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.890
in Japan over financial
charges in 2018, tensions

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.130
between Renault and Nissan
spilled out into the open.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.040
He denies the charges and
eventually fled the country.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.680
- When you took Carlos
Ghosn out of the equation

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.800
there was no real good way for
these companies to cooperate.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.900
And you realize actually
what Ghosn had been doing

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.990
for so many years was refereeing
some kind of catfight.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.570
- [Narrator] Then came further challenges.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.010
- Covid supply chains and we
have a geopolitical situation.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.160
Make the material cost and the hike

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.160
and the cost is going to
the sky rocket situation.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.110
- [Narrator] Renault had
to sell its majority stakes

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.460
in Russia's biggest automaker.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.470
After the Ukraine war broke out

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.110
it capped off more than
two years of losses.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.650
- Two years and a half ago,
we were really in a bad shape.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.740
You know, we lost like 8
billion in Euro in a semester.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.730
So that was like,
- Wow.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.140
So we lost 600 billion and that's red.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.010
- [Narrator] Amid the crisis.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.380
Renault CEO thought there
was also an opportunity

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.110
for the French car maker
to reinvent itself.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.980
- And all the things we are
doing are first to make sure

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.690
that Renault, you know,

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.940
on the next Grand Prix
will be better positioned

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.690
because it will be different rules,

00:02:35.671 --> 00:02:37.500
different technical setup, et cetera.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.210
But it's never done against the, you know

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.770
the alliance or against Nissan.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.740
In fact, they can take advantage
some of our experience.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.930
I think also, and vice versa.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.340
- It became clear to both sides.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.173
They'd be better off

00:02:48.173 --> 00:02:50.220
operating more
independently of each other.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.260
- We had a many things in the past, right?

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:57.260
But we are not doing this like
for sake of the rebalancing

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.410
or you know Nissan
victory, Renault victory

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.330
on the historical items.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.290
- Think we have to sometimes
go back to the original spirit

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.110
which was a very, very
pragmatic collaboration.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.480
That's what we tried to do

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.560
- [Narrator] Under the new agreement.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.240
Renault will reduce its stake
in Nissan from 43% to 15%.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.380
Nissan will also invest

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.840
in Renault's electric vehicle
and software business.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.910
- They can keep cooperating
on certain things

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.520
if they want and if both
parties see the benefit

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.080
or they can go and seek other partners

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.730
if they think they can get a better deal.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.220
- My focus is of course is creating

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.390
the uniqueness of Renault.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.370
That needs to be different from Nissan.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:37.590
They have to have a
different strategy from us.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.423
It's good.

00:03:38.423 --> 00:03:42.360
- So we cannot really do
the business in extension

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.180
from the past way for
the future because the

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.010
circumstance is totally different.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.770
This is why we made this
announcement to go into

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:53.250
the next ear and what
kind of the governance

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.880
that we should have in the
partnership or structure.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.470
- [Narrator] The deal
comes as both companies

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.200
look to new types of
partnerships and batteries.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.883
EV technology and software.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.720
The chip maker Qualcomm
has already said it

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.070
would take a stake in Renault's
new EV business on par

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:13.233
- On par is a very reasonable investment

00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:16.710
with a very strong return
on the capital location

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.720
for Nissan or for any investor

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.070
with very good products
that people are willing to

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.330
you know, pay for.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.440
This is a chance that many
other newcomers coming

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.300
from the outside don't have.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.160
- [Narrator] Renault and
Nissan have said their alliance

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.200
will continue and announce joint projects

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.230
in markets such as
Argentina, Mexico, and India.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.580
- We are setting up the new stage

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.770
for the alliance, how to
collaborate, how to work

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.990
and if there's opportunity, why not?

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.060
- [Narrator] But several
issues remain open.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.160
Nissan did not say how
much it would invest

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.630
in Renault's EV company.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.210
Also under negotiation is
the intellectual property

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.550
that goes into that Renault
venture, which is owned

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.390
by Nissan.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.220
- This is also why it's
difficult for investors

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.040
because there are still some
negotiations to take place.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.803
This isn't like the
complete end of the story.

